<h2 data-fv-section="conflict-inspector" data-fv-advanced="1" data-fv-advanced-group="rules">Rule testing and troubleshooting</h2>
<div class="rules-bottom-grid fv-rules-grid">
    <div class="rules-panel fv-rules-source-panel">
        <div class="rules-header">
            <h3>Test the current rule set</h3>
            <span class="rules-help">Use the same source switch here to test one item, preview all assignments, and inspect conflicts.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fv-rules-source-switch" role="tablist" aria-label="Rules troubleshooting source switcher">
            <button type="button" class="fv-rules-source-btn" data-fv-rules-source-toggle="docker" onclick="setRulesWorkspaceType('docker')"><i class="fa fa-cubes"></i> Docker</button>
            <button type="button" class="fv-rules-source-btn" data-fv-rules-source-toggle="vm" onclick="setRulesWorkspaceType('vm')"><i class="fa fa-desktop"></i> VMs</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rules-panel fv-rule-troubleshoot-panel" data-fv-rules-type="docker">
        <div class="rules-header">
            <h3>Docker troubleshooting</h3>
            <span class="rules-help">Check how a single container would be routed, then inspect the whole Docker rule set.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fv-rule-stage">
            <div class="fv-rule-stage-head">
                <strong>3. Test one item</strong>
                <span>Enter a sample container and see which rule would win first.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="fv-rule-tester-grid">
                <input id="docker-rule-test-name" type="text" placeholder="Test container name (example: media-server)">
                <input id="docker-rule-test-label-key" type="text" placeholder="Test label key (optional)">
                <input id="docker-rule-test-label-value" type="text" placeholder="Test label value (optional)">
                <input id="docker-rule-test-image" type="text" placeholder="Test image (optional, example: linuxserver/sonarr)">
                <input id="docker-rule-test-compose" type="text" placeholder="Test compose project (optional)">
            </div>
            <div class="rule-test-samples">
                <button type="button" onclick="applyRuleTestSample('docker','media')"><i class="fa fa-flask"></i> Media sample</button>
                <button type="button" onclick="applyRuleTestSample('docker','network')"><i class="fa fa-flask"></i> Network sample</button>
                <button type="button" onclick="applyRuleTestSample('docker','database')"><i class="fa fa-flask"></i> Database sample</button>
            </div>
            <div class="fv-rule-test-actions">
                <button type="button" onclick="testAutoRule('docker')"><i class="fa fa-crosshairs"></i> Test rule priority</button>
                <button type="button" onclick="runRuleSimulator('docker')"><i class="fa fa-list-alt"></i> Preview all assignments</button>
            </div>
            <div id="docker-rule-validation" class="inline-validation-hint"></div>
            <div id="docker-rule-test-output" class="rule-test-output">Enter a test container name to see which Docker rule wins.</div>
            <pre id="docker-rule-sim-output" class="diagnostics-output compact-output">Preview all Docker assignments to review the full rule outcome.</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="fv-rule-stage">
            <div class="fv-rule-stage-head">
                <strong>4. Inspect conflicts</strong>
                <span>See why Docker items are assigned, where overlaps exist, and which exclude rules are blocking matches.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="fv-rule-test-actions">
                <button type="button" onclick="runConflictInspector('docker')"><i class="fa fa-search"></i> Scan Docker conflicts</button>
            </div>
